cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AgentWire (swarmwire): Compact Binary Wire Protocol and Verifiable Policy Runtime for Multi-Agent AI Systems"
message: "If you use AgentWire (swarmwire) in research, benchmarks, or production systems, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Pandey"
    given-names: "Alok"
    alias: "alok-108"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alok-108/agentwire"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/swarmwire/"
abstract: >-
  AgentWire (published on PyPI as swarmwire) is a compact, cryptographically
  verifiable binary wire protocol (AW01) and deterministic policy runtime for
  multi-agent AI systems, featuring a Rust core with PyO3 bindings, constant-time
  HMAC-SHA256 frame authentication with replay protection, two-phase Reserve/Settle
  budget accounting, a networked TCP RPC transport, and a 1:1 lossless live trace
  decompiler.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - multi-agent-systems
  - binary-protocol
  - rpc
  - rust
  - pyo3
  - policy-engine
  - observability
license: Apache-2.0
